---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import profileImage from "@/assets/profile.jpg";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/container.astro";
import Sectionhead from "@/components/sectionhead.astro";
---

<Layout title="About">
  <Container>
    <Sectionhead>
      <Fragment slot="title">About</Fragment>
      <Fragment slot="desc">
        The person and ideas behind PatternBloom
      </Fragment>
    </Sectionhead>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl mt-20 grid gap-6">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-[var(--color-coral)] pl-8 bg-white/90 p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          What is PatternBloom?
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/70 mt-3">
          PatternBloom is a personal brand for procedural art projects. It’s a space to share generative designs, open-source tools, and experiments at the intersection of code and visual art.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-[var(--color-sunny)] pl-8 bg-white/90 p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          How the Art Is Made
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/70 mt-3">
          All the work on PatternBloom is created using generative and procedural techniques, primarily with the p5.js library. This involves writing code to produce designs through mathematical rules, randomness, and algorithms. Unlike AI-generated art, procedural art is rooted in the direct control of the artist, blending logic and creativity to produce unique, intentional pieces.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/70 mt-3">
          This approach allows for infinite possibilities while ensuring every piece is thoughtfully crafted.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-l-4 border-[var(--color-mint)] pl-8 bg-white/90 p-8">
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          About the Author
        </h2>
        <div class="mt-4 hidden md:block max-w-[200px]">
          <Picture
            src={profileImage}
            alt="Elena Torró"
            widths={[200, 400]}
            loading="eager"
            format="avif"
            class="grayscale hover:grayscale-0 transition-all duration-500"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/70 mt-4">
          PatternBloom is the creative outlet of Elena Torró, a software engineer from Murcia, Spain, who is passionate about generative art, open source, and the fascinating intersection of art and technology. Through PatternBloom, Elena combines her technical expertise and artistic curiosity to explore procedural techniques and share the results.
        </p>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/70 mt-3">
          You can find more at <a href="https://elenatorro.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-[var(--color-coral)] font-semibold hover:underline">elenatorro.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
